This project implements local ComfyUI inference support for SenseNova-U1.5.
It is a fork: the node pack comes from one upstream project, the quantization
stack was ported from another. Both are credited below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Code provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Base (node pack, bf16 path, checkpoint contract, examples, tests):
- T8mars/Comfyui-SenseNova-U1.5-Wrapper-T8, taken at version 1.3.6
  https://github.com/T8mars/Comfyui-SenseNova-U1.5-Wrapper-T8
- Copyright T8mars (T8star) contributors; Apache License 2.0
- Kept from upstream and not reimplemented here: the 1.3.4 pure-PyTorch
  split-half RoPE fix and the 1.3.5 1116-tensor checkpoint contract
  (checkpoint_contract.json) with file-size, storage-dtype and
  legacy-revision validation.

Ported (all quantized / ConvRot code paths):
- Milor123/ComfyUI-SenseNova-U1.5-ConvRot at commit 7e1e320
  https://github.com/Milor123/ComfyUI-SenseNova-U1.5-ConvRot
- Copyright Milor123 contributors; Apache License 2.0
- Ported files and logic: sensenova_u15/quant_bridge.py,
  sensenova_u15/qt_guards.py, the quant detection and per-format contract in
  sensenova_u15/loader.py, the custom_operations hook in
  sensenova_u15/model_config.py, and tools/convert_sensenova_int4_convrot.py,
  tools/make_hybrid_ladder.py, tools/inject_sensenova_metadata.py.
- Not taken: Milor123's checkpoint_contract.py (BASE_CONTRACT). Quantized
  validation here is derived from the upstream JSON contract so the file-size,
  final_legacy and SFT checks survive.

Changes made by this fork (Spirindzhiukas/Comfyui-SenseNova-U1.5-Wrapper-T8-ANT-fork):
- CRLF-tolerant tokenizer asset validation (.gitattributes pins LF)
- English UI labels, defaults, frontend extension and example workflows
- English-first documentation layout (README.md / README_CN.md)
- Quantization wiring (model_config.quant_config, comfy.utils.convert_old_quants)
  and a post-load QuantizedTensor invariant
- Measured comfy-kitchen INT8 convrot capability probe instead of a version check
- Capability-aware ConvRot bridge and lazy installation of the cast guards
- --variant auto in the metadata injector; Windows path cleanups in the tools
- See memory.md and the "Credits and provenance" section of README.md.

Third-party methods and runtimes used through their public interfaces:
- ConvRot - Hanzuliang et al.; technical notes in
  https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI/issues/14735
- Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen - quantized tensor runtimes (Apache-2.0)
- silveroxides/convert_to_quant - converter lineage behind the quantization
  scripts (via Milor123)
- ComfyUI (Comfy-Org) - used through its public model, node, sampling,
  attention, operation and model-management interfaces.

